  "question": {
    "text": "The power of a lens (biconvex) is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> in particular medium. Refractive index of the lens is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;and radii of curvature are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> respectively. The refractive index of surrounding medium:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Using Len&#39;s maker formula,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is refractive index of lens and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is of surrounding medium.&nbsp;</p><p>Putting the values,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>08</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>The refractive index of surrounding medium is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>.</p></blockquote>"
  }
